01:22:25.360 --> 01:22:29.840 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Thank you, Mayor Collins, members of the
city council. Dan Dorsch, executive

01:22:28.400 --> 01:22:35.440 align:start position:19%
director for Habitat for Humanity of
Laram County. In early 2024, Magic City

01:22:33.440 --> 01:22:40.080 align:start position:19%
approached Habitat uh to seeing if there
is some way we could partner. And I

01:22:37.920 --> 01:22:43.120 align:start position:19%
said, "Let's talk." So, we sat down and
Magic City told us that they were

01:22:41.840 --> 01:22:46.880 align:start position:19%
looking at changing the way they were
providing their services to their folks.

01:22:44.960 --> 01:22:50.719 align:start position:19%
They were going from a group setting and
wanting to go to more independent living

01:22:48.639 --> 01:22:55.120 align:start position:19%
for those who are able, providing more
dignity for their folks. And they said,

01:22:53.360 --> 01:22:58.480 align:start position:19%
"We have land, but we don't know how to
build. Is there some way Habitat and

01:22:56.800 --> 01:23:01.600 align:start position:19%
Magic City can work together?" And we
said, "Let's talk."

01:23:00.159 --> 01:23:07.280 align:start position:19%
And over the course of the next year and
a half, we decided to try to put to not

01:23:04.639 --> 01:23:11.760 align:start position:19%
try, we're putting together a project on
the northeast corner of Ridge and

01:23:08.960 --> 01:23:16.000 align:start position:19%
Charles, uh, just off, uh, north of
Persing, just east of Ridge Road. And

01:23:14.239 --> 01:23:22.159 align:start position:19%
Charles, that section of Charles is a
dirt road. And we said, this is let's

01:23:20.159 --> 01:23:25.520 align:start position:19%
let's look at this this lot, this
section to build on. And so putting our

01:23:23.760 --> 01:23:30.000 align:start position:19%
minds together, we came up with Magic
Meadows as the name for this project.

01:23:27.520 --> 01:23:34.480 align:start position:19%
And it will provide 12 units, half
habitat, half magic city of uh an

01:23:32.800 --> 01:23:37.440 align:start position:19%
inclusive community living together in
this little neighborhood on the corner

01:23:35.600 --> 01:23:41.840 align:start position:19%
of Ridge and Charles. And it's an
amazing opportunity for us uh as

01:23:40.080 --> 01:23:45.600 align:start position:19%
partners in the nonprofit world to come
together. We often work together, but

01:23:43.360 --> 01:23:49.040 align:start position:19%
not in this capacity. in doing some
research when we were putting this

01:23:47.280 --> 01:23:53.360 align:start position:19%
project together, we haven't found uh
another project anywhere in the country

01:23:51.520 --> 01:23:58.400 align:start position:19%
that brings this type of nonprofit
partnership together to build homes for

01:23:55.360 --> 01:24:04.000 align:start position:19%
both Magic City folks and Habitat. And
what's really cool about this is as we

01:24:00.080 --> 01:24:07.920 align:start position:19%
were working through this project, it um
first of all, I should say, I apologize

01:24:05.760 --> 01:24:12.400 align:start position:19%
some when I said half Magic City, half
Habitat, it would be um most of Magic

01:24:10.400 --> 01:24:16.880 align:start position:19%
City's folks live in a rental unit.
Habitat as some of you are well aware of

01:24:14.560 --> 01:24:20.320 align:start position:19%
are home ownership opportunities.
What may happen through this project is

01:24:18.560 --> 01:24:24.000 align:start position:19%
that some of Magic Cities may qualify
for home ownership. So not only do they

01:24:22.159 --> 01:24:28.239 align:start position:19%
have the dignity of living independently
but be through our program and through

01:24:26.480 --> 01:24:34.000 align:start position:19%
our partnership have the opportunity for
home ownership, furthering their

01:24:29.760 --> 01:24:37.040 align:start position:19%
dignity. So, this this application um is
similar for those of you who were on

01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:41.040 align:start position:19%
city council when you approved the one
for Pong Horn Crossing um which I'm

01:24:39.360 --> 01:24:48.239 align:start position:19%
proud to say is almost finished with
infrastructure. Uh this infrastructure

01:24:43.840 --> 01:24:52.719 align:start position:19%
is way less intensive than um Pong Horn
Crossing because of a couple things.

01:24:50.560 --> 01:24:58.560 align:start position:19%
One, this is an infill lot that has sat
unused for multiple years. Um, we are

01:24:55.440 --> 01:25:02.000 align:start position:19%
getting 12 units on just4 acres of land,
taking advantage of the cottage lot

01:25:00.080 --> 01:25:06.080 align:start position:19%
amendment for that the city approved
several years ago through the UDC. So,

01:25:04.400 --> 01:25:11.120 align:start position:19%
we are taking advantage of that infill
lot, adding units where there haven't

01:25:08.480 --> 01:25:15.040 align:start position:19%
presently been units. Because it is an
infill lot, it is already surrounded by

01:25:12.880 --> 01:25:18.639 align:start position:19%
city road and infrastructure. Instead of
having to bring sewer hundreds of feet

01:25:17.040 --> 01:25:22.239 align:start position:19%
like we did with Ponghorn Crossing, it
is already in Charles in the alley

01:25:20.080 --> 01:25:26.480 align:start position:19%
directly behind the property. So the
resolution stated for 500,000 is much

01:25:24.639 --> 01:25:30.400 align:start position:19%
less than for Pong Horn Crossing. It'll
be much easier for us as an organization

01:25:28.239 --> 01:25:35.600 align:start position:19%
to manage this project with those grant
funds. And um we greatly appreciate the

01:25:33.360 --> 01:25:40.159 align:start position:19%
city support not only for this project
but for affordable housing as it is a

01:25:37.520 --> 01:25:45.199 align:start position:19%
huge need in this community. Presently I
believe there are between 800 and 900

01:25:42.080 --> 01:25:49.840 align:start position:19%
folks waiting on the uh housing waiting
list for affordable housing in Cheyenne

01:25:46.960 --> 01:25:53.600 align:start position:19%
alone at the housing authority. So, the
more we can do to add those affordable

01:25:51.360 --> 01:25:57.120 align:start position:19%
units, the better. Um, and again, this
is an amazing opportunity and a

01:25:55.040 --> 01:26:00.960 align:start position:19%
partnership for Magic City and Habitat
to build community and hope in our in

01:25:59.199 --> 01:26:03.920 align:start position:19%
our city. Thank you very much. And I
stand for any questions.

01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:07.120 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Thanks, Dan. And I remember a year and a
half ago or so, we were talking about,

01:26:05.760 --> 01:26:11.520 align:start position:19%
